From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:27:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test(kanban): the draining-pin test's body operates
 the Desktop backend, so it still gives a local marker

Main's 3ea3e88ece added test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py with the body "Inspect the Desktop backend's ... on the MacBook.", which pinned only through the body marker this PR makes title-only (CI run 43170686823, shard 6/8: 'home gateway marker' != 'local marker'). The body now restarts the Desktop backend before inspecting, an operate instruction the new rule keeps local; the test's intent (a local-marker hub pin offered and claimed when the hub is not draining) is unchanged.

Proof: on the merge 7cfc9a9e0a the file fails 1 test; with this body, 43 files referencing kanban_placement/kanban_tools_placement: 1255 passed, 0 failed (includes this file); tests/gateway/test_delivery_unknown_target.py 3 passed; scripts/check --base origin/main ok. hermes_cli/kanban_placement.py is unchanged on main since the merge-base, so the replay (10455 cards: 90 lose the pin, 0 gain) still holds.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py
index f09551cb17..e08f5e2325 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_draining_machine_pin.py
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@ from tests.hermes_cli.kanban_sync_fake_board import FakeService
 from tests.hermes_cli.test_kanban_worker_node import HUB, MACHINES, Gateway, _tool_create
 
 MAC = "macbook"
-BODY = "Inspect the Desktop backend's ~/.hermes/state.db and ~/.hermes/logs/gateway.log on the MacBook."
+# An operate instruction: a body that only names "the Desktop backend" no longer pins (PR 1222). [daveey]
+BODY = "Restart the Desktop backend, then inspect ~/.hermes/state.db and ~/.hermes/logs/gateway.log on the MacBook."
 
 
 @pytest.fixture
